  (text "Design notes (Pango UG040012 Logos2 Hardware Design Guide V1.4):" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 190 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "be6976b8-3cf7-44b9-adce-a22e2a987afa")
  )
  (text "- VCC and VCC_DRM share one 1.0 V supply (2.3.1). VCCA 1.8 V. All I/O banks and VCCIOCFG at 3.3 V." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 193.6 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "b004418c-b39e-4428-b76a-854568e6b13a")
  )
  (text "- Master SPI at 3.3 V: VCCIOCFG = 3.3 V, VCCIOL5 = 3.3 V, VCCIOL4 not floating, SCBV tied to VCCIOCFG (Table 2-1). MODE[2:0] = 001 (3.2)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 197.2 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "b9131067-ffdc-40a7-8a0c-b16da1188861")
  )
  (text "- PG2L50H FBG484 decoupling (Table 2-3): VCC 3x100u, 6x4.7u, 8x0.47u, 5x0.1u; VCC_DRM 1x100u, 2x0.47u, 2x0.1u; VCCA 1x47u, 3x4.7u, 5x0.47u, 2x0.1u;" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 200.79999999999998 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "3f78eaed-472c-4aa3-b7d7-d20ca63ac67c")
  )
  (text "  VCCIOCFG 1x47u, 1x0.47u, 1x0.1u; VCCIO 2x47u, 2x4.7u, 4x0.47u, 2x0.1u per bank (47u may be reduced when banks share a supply). Parts per Table 2-6." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 204.39999999999998 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "f1af8392-aae1-496f-98c8-c81c7b0bd5ae")
  )
  (text "- VCCB (battery-backed key memory) not used: tie to VCCA (Table 9-2). Keys live in eFuse." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 207.99999999999997 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "3a83c480-0521-424a-9e73-6ebc8615f617")
  )
  (text "- HSSTLP not used: HSSTAVCC and HSSTAVCCPLL floating with a grounding-resistor position each; HSSTRX* and HSSTRREF to GND; HSSTREFCLK and HSSTTX floating (Table 5-1)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 211.59999999999997 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "36dfc71c-76e3-485c-998f-349deb4198a5")
  )
  (text "- Main clock on a GMCLK pin, P side only for a single-ended oscillator (9.1). Do not use the N side of a clock-output pair as a general input (9.3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 215.19999999999996 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "19a92572-23ee-4a56-89d7-efe10ed5f3e7")
  )
  (text "- Power: 5 V always on. 3V3_AO LDO powers the RTC and the power-control logic; the TPM is on the switched 3V3 (all its state is non-volatile). Switchers are enabled by WAKE (FPGA), the pushbutton, or the RTC alarm;" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 218.79999999999995 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "f17f8ebd-b6a9-4f29-bd4b-0bc4dcdec67b")
  )
  (text "  the FPGA asserts WAKE early in the boot ROM and drops it to power down after programming the next alarm. RTC /INT is open-drain and is not reset by a VDD cycle." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 222.39999999999995 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "f208276f-2007-4e8e-94f6-3862be6064f9")
  )
  (text "- JTAG header and test points are not populated in production; JTAG is permanently disabled at enrollment (JTAGLOCK, SCANLOCK)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12 225.99999999999994 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
    (uuid "cafcc886-f2e9-4d63-bc63-91b69e753cd2")
  )
